{#- Who acts, and the assistant's part. Shared by the brain's deciders of what work exists (the day decider, the
    shadow concern decider); docs/design/brain_delegates_work_2026-10-04.md. Expects `owner`. -#}
Every piece of work names who acts: the assistant, {{ owner }}, or another person by name; the assistant's part (the
act itself, or tell, remind, ask or check, with what); and when (a local time, or now). A standing wish that the
assistant does something at a time is the assistant's act at that time. When the work is {{ owner }}'s own or another
person's, the assistant's part is to tell, remind, ask or check, at a time it helps. Say what should be done and who
does it, never how: dayflow plans how.
